--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-qcom-battmgr-uke-control
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-qcom-battmgr-uke-control
@@ -102,3 +102,28 @@ Description:
                 Xiaomi raw property, USB current, PD/QC/PPS/EPR negotiation or
                 factory/calibration API is exposed. Firmware owns CV and all
                 autonomous protections. This driver is not a real-time cutoff.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_settings
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                Root-readable (0400), CAP_SYS_ADMIN, Uke threshold build only.
+                Deliberate firmware read, unlike metadata-only uke_charge_state.
+                Reads only the three OEM standard threshold fields (wire25/26/27),
+                using the existing serialized and matched GET transport. No FCC,
+                voltage, Xiaomi property, setter, lease or service activation.
+                An unexpired control lease or busy driver rejects the query.
+                At most one attempt per second, three GETs without replay, stop
+                at the first error/lifecycle change; no partial result. Invalid
+                booleans/percentages, changed epochs or a batch older than three
+                seconds fail. No verified configuration cache is renewed.
+
+                Version1 line:
+                version instance generation firmware_epoch source_epoch
+                  received_boottime_ns reported_enabled reported_start reported_end
+
+                Successful readback reports firmware settings only. It does not
+                qualify their electrical effect, autonomous protection, pack
+                profile, battery isolation or a control permission. In particular,
+                disabled thresholds are not converted to invented0/100 settings.
+                Existing standard threshold clients still require admission.
